.TH DIGICARLO 1 "2026-09-23" "DigiCarlo 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
digicarlo \- get the pictures off old digital cameras, with dates that are right
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B digicarlo
.I COMMAND
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B digicarlo
takes pictures and clips off memory cards, USB cameras and the SiPix StyleCam
Blink II, and dates them by when they came off the camera rather than by the
camera's clock, keeping the gaps between shots that the clock still measures
correctly.
.PP
Work happens in two steps. A \fIpull\fR copies every new file into the
\fIarchive\fR, byte for byte, reading each copy back before it counts. To
\fIdevelop\fR puts re-dated copies in the \fIlibrary\fR: EXIF and QuickTime
dates set, and MOV, AVI and MTS clips remuxed to MP4 with the video stream
copied untouched. \fBimport\fR does both, asking before it writes to the
library.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B import \fR[\fISOURCE\fR...]
Pull from every camera and card plugged in (or those named), show the dates
waiting shots will get, and on a yes develop them.
.TP
.B sources
List the cameras and cards plugged in, numbered for use as \fISOURCE\fR.
.TP
.B pull \fR[\fISOURCE\fR...]
Copy new files into the archive only.
.TP
.B plan
Show the sessions waiting shots fall into and the dates they would get.
.TP
.B develop
Put waiting shots in the library.
.TP
.B skip \fISHOTS\fR...
Leave shots out of the library (they stay in the archive).
\fBunskip\fR [\fINAME\fR...] brings them back.
.TP
.B remember \fIDIR\fR...
Record everything already in \fIDIR\fR so a pull never brings in a second copy.
Useful once, on a library filled before DigiCarlo.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the tools and folders DigiCarlo relies on, and what is plugged in. For
the SiPix Blink II it also runs Blinky's link checks.
.TP
.B config \fR[\fBset\fR \fIKEY VALUE\fR]
Show or change settings: \fBlibrary\fR, \fBarchive\fR, \fBmax_gap_days\fR,
\fBsession_spacing_seconds\fR, \fBstill_format\fR, \fBjpeg_quality\fR,
\fBaac_bitrate\fR.
.TP
.B update \fR[\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-install\fR]
Fetch a newer release from GitHub, verified against its published SHA256SUMS.
.SH DATES
A \fIsession\fR is a run of shots over which the camera's clock ran unbroken; a
new one starts where the clock went backwards (a battery swap resetting it) or
leapt forward more than \fBmax_gap_days\fR. By default a pull's last shot is
dated when it came off the camera and sessions are stacked back from there,
\fBsession_spacing_seconds\fR apart.
.PP
\fB\-\-date\fR changes that, and may be repeated; later ones win:
.TP
.B \-\-date \(dq2026-09-12 19:00\(dq
Everything starts then.
.TP
.B \-\-date S2=\(dq2026-09-12 19:00\(dq
Session 2 starts then. \fBS2-S4=\fR... runs sessions 2 to 4 one after another.
.TP
.B \-\-date 12-30=\(dqyesterday 18:00\(dq
Shots 12 to 30 start then.
.TP
.B \-\-date S3=camera
Keep the camera's own dates.
.PP
Times may be \fIYYYY-MM-DD HH:MM[:SS]\fR, a bare date (noon), \fBnow\fR,
\fBtoday\fR or \fByesterday\fR with an optional time. Session and shot numbers
are the ones \fBdigicarlo plan\fR prints.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-from \fIDIR\fR
Pull from a folder as if it were a card.
.TP
.B \-\-library \fIDIR\fR, \fB\-\-archive \fIDIR\fR
Override the folders from the settings for this run.
.TP
.B \-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes
Do not ask before writing to the library.
.TP
.B \-\-shots
List every shot in the plan, not just sessions.
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR; \fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet
Say more, or less.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/digicarlo/digicarlo.conf
Settings.
.TP
.I ARCHIVE/manifest.jsonl
What has been pulled and developed. Append-only JSON lines.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR digicarlo-gui (1),
.BR exiftool (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR gphoto2 (1)
